[00:34.48] I imagine the gracious,
[00:38.79] Benevolent ritual of Death.
[00:47.01] Grave and porcelain,
[00:49.50] With baby blue lips and pale pink eyes,
[00:55.22] Descending toward me.
[01:28.29] Her glowing hands cradled at my head
[01:36.06] And knees submerging me into waves of icy seas.
[01:55.12] I imagine the end.
[04:02.33] Then further downward so that I can rest,
[04:13.65] Cocooned by the heat of the ocean floor.
[04:25.70] In the dark, my flesh to disintegrate
[05:56.21] Into consumption for the earth.
